{
  "name": "openrouter-endpoints",
  "kind": "endpoints",
  "source": "OpenRouter's public endpoint list per model, GET https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/models/<author>/<slug>/endpoints (no key), each endpoint's provider_name, tag, quantization, its supported_parameters (seed: whether they hold seed), and pricing.prompt, pricing.completion and pricing.input_cache_read in dollars per token, multiplied here by one million",
  "fetched": "2026-11-26",
  "unit": "US dollars per million tokens",
  "rule": "Pre-registration, Models: each model and both judges pinned to the maker's own endpoint where OpenRouter lists one, otherwise the cheapest endpoint that honours seed, with allow_fallbacks false. A maker's endpoint that does not honour seed does not qualify (the lead's answer of 2026-11-26, \"Seed first\"; AGENTS.md rule 6: every sampled call is seeded). Cheapest is the lowest cost of price_weights' tokens at the endpoint's input and output prices. A pin is openrouter_provider {order: [tag], allow_fallbacks: false, require_parameters: true}: OpenRouter then refuses a call the endpoint cannot honour in full, the seed among its parameters, rather than dropping one.",
  "price_weights": {
    "source": "research/results/h1-cost.json, tokens.gatemem.high: the H1 GateMem arm's high estimate of answer tokens, the largest run on M1",
    "input": 738446778.602545,
    "output": 2324463.418884
  },
  "notes": [
    "Each response was read once on the day fetched, saved as served beside this file (response) and hashed (response_sha256); the endpoint list is volatile, and an endpoint gone on the day of a run fails that run's first call under allow_fallbacks false, which is the registered behaviour: the list is read again and the new pin is its own PR, before the run starts.",
    "deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro-0813: the maker's own endpoint (DeepSeek, tag deepseek) does not list seed among its supported parameters, so it does not qualify; of the thirteen endpoints that honour seed, Wafer's wafer/us (mxfp4) costs least at price_weights' token mix, about 92 dollars against 220 for Wafer's wafer/mxfp4 and 433 for the first one not quantised to 4 bits as listed, Alibaba's alibaba (quantization unknown), and M1 is pinned to it (decision 2026-11-26-r6-decision-m1-cheapest-seeded-endpoint). It serves a 4-bit quantisation of M1.",
    "openai/gpt-5.4: OpenAI lists three endpoints of its own (openai, openai/flex, openai/fast); B1 is pinned to the standard tier, tag openai (decision 2026-11-26-r6-decision-b1-standard-tier).",
    "Prices are each endpoint's list price on the day fetched, not what the ledger meters (pi-ai's catalogue price, model.cost) and not a quote."
  ],
  "sent_parameters": {
    "source": "What pi-ai 1.3.0 puts in the request body for each call the runner makes (api/openai-completions.js, buildParams), in OpenRouter's parameter names: the answer turn sends seed (samplingParams), tools when the condition gives the agent memory tools, and reasoning ({effort: none}, thinking off, for a reasoning model on OpenRouter's thinking format: M1 and GPT-5.4); the MEM-INV-Bench note call sends seed, temperature, max_tokens and reasoning; the lint call sends seed, temperature, max_tokens, response_format (a json_schema, so structured_outputs) and reasoning; GateMem's judge sends seed, temperature, max_tokens, response_format and structured_outputs; LongMemEval's judge sends seed, temperature and max_tokens. pi-ai names the token limit max_completion_tokens, read here as OpenRouter's max_tokens; that OpenRouter checks it as max_tokens under require_parameters is not checked offline, and a refusal of the first call stops the run, the safe direction. With require_parameters true OpenRouter routes only to an endpoint whose supported_parameters hold every one of these, so a pinned endpoint must list them all.",
    "answer": ["max_tokens", "reasoning", "seed", "tools"],
    "note": ["max_tokens", "reasoning", "seed", "temperature"],
    "lint": [
      "max_tokens",
      "reasoning",
      "response_format",
      "seed",
      "structured_outputs",
      "temperature"
    ],
    "gatemem_judge": ["max_tokens", "response_format", "seed", "structured_outputs", "temperature"],
    "longmemeval_judge": ["max_tokens", "seed", "temperature"]
  },
